In article <90303.103959U3A@psuvm.psu.edu>, U3A@psuvm.psu.edu writes:
>I would greatly appreciate any help anyone could give me with a game called
>Larn.  It is a dungeon game similar to Hack.  After we added an EGA moniter
>to our system, the graphics for Larn no longer work properly.  Instead of the
>usual game screen, the program displays the numerical location of the cursor.
>Is there an EGA version of Larn, or is there a way to tell the program that
>an EGA system is in use.
>                                 Thanks for any and all sugestions,
>                                 Jim

It's not the EGA that's the problem, you need to have ANSI.Sys loaded in 
your Config.Sys. (Assuming that you are running MSDOS, of course.) Add it 
in your Config.Sys like this:

device=c:\dos\ansi.sys

This assumes that you have Ansi.Sys in your C:\Dos subdirectory. Also, add 
it to your existing Config.Sys file. 

You can also use NAnsi.Sys, FConsole.Dev and others (I use FConsole.Dev on 
my PC and NAnsi.Sys on my laptop).

Of course, if it's not MSDOS ... Nevermind :-)

